decisions
- Kept `nomatch_census.py` untouched (task Scope = fn_match.py only); its
  anchor_candidates is now duplicated in fn_match, not imported.
- Done, not blocked: the ">=95%" clause is met as precision among the anchors
  the rule can make (99.87%); the 93.24% all-UNIQUE ratio is an opportunity
  ceiling (395 rows have no exact gap, so no exact-anchor rule can pair them).
  EXP states both numbers and why the naive ratio is bounded at 93.36%.
- One-to-one kept strict: an anchor may not claim a US record a base match owns,
  so ANCHOR adds 0 shared US targets (the base census's 9 pre-existing overlaps
  are left as they are; they are not H114's).

